# JavaScript Conventions — Stimulus (Hotwire)

## Import Maps
- JavaScript bundled via **<%= js_engine %>**
- Pin dependencies in `config/importmap.rb`
- No build step required for JavaScript

## Stimulus Controllers
- One controller per file in `app/javascript/controllers/`
- Name files as `feature_controller.js` (snake_case)
- Register controllers via `index.js`

## Naming
- Controllers: `data-controller="feature-name"` (kebab-case in HTML)
- Targets: `data-feature-name-target="element"` (camelCase target name)
- Actions: `data-action="event->controller#method"`
- Values: `data-feature-name-value-name="..."` (kebab-case)

## Turbo
- Use Turbo Drive for page navigation (enabled by default)
- Use Turbo Frames for partial page updates
- Use Turbo Streams for real-time updates
- Disable Turbo selectively with `data-turbo="false"` when needed

## CSS
- Bootstrap for styling
- Custom styles in `app/assets/stylesheets/`

## Testing
- System tests with Capybara for full integration
- Keep JavaScript logic minimal; prefer server-side rendering
